    <title subtitle="" lang="en">A City in Two Continents</title>
    <description lang="en">This virtual learning object "A City in Two Continents" that makes part of the lesson No: 5, Sally on the Aegean Sea, which in turn belongs to the Elementary (A2.2) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, is intended to work on: ask and say where places are in a country. The grammar of this LO refers to: adjectives and nouns to describe a city, e.g. modern, aqueduct; simple future tense using will, may, and might, e.g. we will also visit Topkapi Palace; simple past tense, regular and irregular verbs in affirmative, e.g. the builders covered the interior walls with blue tiles. Also, the vocabulary considers: past time expressions, e.g. one time, once; shops, places in towns and cities, e.g. aqueduct, residence.</description>
    <keyword lang="en">
      <li>Using past time expressions</li>
      <li>Simple past tense</li>
      <li>Talking about cities</li>
      <li>Places in the city</li>
      <li>Talking about things in the future</li>
      <li>Talking about actions in the future</li>
      <li>Talking about events in the future</li>
      <li>Future tense</li>
      <li>Adjectives</li>
    </keyword>
  </general>
